{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J2", "U9", "U10"],
      "pins": ["J2.2", "J2.3", "U9.MH2", "U10.2"],
      "nets": ["BAT+ (unlabeled rail at VBUS/C5/IC2-VIN)", "NET0041 (battery negative)"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet, the barrel-jack J2 (Barrel_Jack_Switch) is wired so that its sleeve contact pin 2 joins the BAT+ rail (the same node as USB VBUS, C5 top plate and IC2 pin A2/VIN), while its switch contact pin 3 joins NET0041, which is the battery negative (U9 pin MH2, and the diode U10 side that feeds the BAT- path). The in-sheet text note still reads '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug'.",
      "expected": "Per the specification the jack must be wired pin1->BAT+ (center), pin2->GND (sleeve), pin3->BAT-; the normally-closed 2-3 contact then ties the battery return to GND when no plug is inserted and breaks it when a plug is inserted. Pin 2 must NOT be on BAT+.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Netlist: J4.1->BAT+ (center/positive), J4.2->GND (sleeve), J4.3->BAT-. Since pins 2 and 3 are normally shorted (per the note) ... this means the jack's internal switch keeps the battery's return path connected to GND by default"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "commit a1d9676 'Meshinger 1.0 rev B WARNING THE DC PLUG PINS ARE WRONG, SHORTS BATTERY!'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EthernetAndPower sheet: J2 'Barrel Jack Switch' pin 2 wire runs to the BAT+ rail shared with J1 VBUS and C5/IC2-VIN; pin 3 wire runs to NET0041 (U9 MH2 battery negative); note '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug'"}
      ],
      "impact": "With no DC plug inserted the jack's closed 2-3 contact directly shorts the battery positive (BAT+) to the battery negative (NET0041), exactly the 'SHORTS BATTERY' failure the spec warns about; additionally the battery return is never connected to GND, so the board cannot power up and the cell/holder is exposed to a hard short.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The board is otherwise a faithful (re-numbered) implementation of the spec, but the DC barrel jack J2 is miswired: its sleeve pin 2 is tied to the BAT+ rail instead of GND, so the normally-closed 2-3 contact shorts BAT+ to the battery-negative net (NET0041) when no plug is inserted, reproducing the documented 'DC plug pins are wrong, shorts battery' fault."
}

